        "runId": "submit-9e9cff89-eaf8-4da3-b719-163cca50324d-07",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "\n\n## Trip highlights\n\nThe first few days introduce you to San José and the Central Mountain Range. You’ll then see the Poás crater and walk the trails at La Paz Waterfall Gardens.\n\nIn the Arenal area, visit the Mistico hanging bridges, take a boat trip on the Frío River in the Caño Negro Wildlife Refuge, and visit a chocolate farm and the Baldi hot springs.\n\nIn Monteverde, explore the cloud forest and visit a family farm that grows coffee and sugarcane. At Selvatura, you’ll find a canopy tour, a butterfly garden, reptiles and amphibians, and a sloth sanctuary.\n\nAfter several days of sightseeing, the route reaches the Pacific coast. Days 10 to 14 are at your leisure, so you can relax by the sea and choose any optional activities that interest you.\n\n\n"
